by wachterjohannes at 2026-08-21T17:57:50Z

Agreed with @OskarStark, and the current config shape backs it up: `tools:` is already a heterogeneous scalar list taking service ids, FQCNs, namespace prefixes and `*`. A tag form can be added later purely additively, say `#foo` or `tag:foo`, without changing what any existing value means and without a second BC break. So deferring costs nothing and locks nothing in.

The uniqueness point is the substantive one. DI tags are global strings, so `foo` from two vendors collide, while FQCN and namespace-prefix filtering is unambiguous by construction. That is exactly why a tag design needs a naming convention of its own, and why it should not be bolted onto a 45-file PR that already carries a BC break.

@Toflar the grouping-across-vendors use case is real though, worth an issue so it does not get lost.

